WEBVTT

00:11.470 --> 00:17.560
(Episode 18:
King's Order)

00:21.830 --> 00:23.950
Hey. Hope you don't mind a visit.

00:25.170 --> 00:26.490
Benwood?

00:26.830 --> 00:27.840
What's going on?

00:27.840 --> 00:29.990
Some urgent business came up.

00:42.130 --> 00:49.100
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:04.520 --> 02:07.630
Have a seat right here.
I'll take your coat.

02:08.010 --> 02:12.010
I am deeply obliged, Yuke Feldio.

02:15.770 --> 02:16.170
(King of Welmelia Vincent V)

02:16.170 --> 02:18.220
(King of Welmelia Vincent V)
Your Majesty King Vincent!

02:18.220 --> 02:21.170
(King of Welmelia Vincent V)
Oh, none of that, please.

02:21.170 --> 02:22.770
(King of Welmelia Vincent V)
I'm undercover today.

02:23.050 --> 02:25.770
I'm here simply as Benwood's friend.

02:25.770 --> 02:28.150
Please feel free to call me Beecha.

02:28.500 --> 02:29.280
Yes, Your Majesty...

02:29.730 --> 02:31.660
Wait, no, I could never do that!

02:32.000 --> 02:34.770
Really, it's okay to loosen up.

02:34.770 --> 02:37.910
This guy's basically Saga's
kid brother, you know.

02:37.910 --> 02:39.410
"This guy"?

02:39.410 --> 02:43.540
In other words, you're like
a younger brother to me, as well.

02:43.540 --> 02:45.920
Please, I'm not worthy of such...

02:45.920 --> 02:49.960
And that also means Beecha's
a disciple of mine.

02:49.960 --> 02:52.550
Now, Benwood, I'm not so sure about that.

03:01.150 --> 03:03.280
Hello, Guild Master.

03:03.280 --> 03:05.820
And your companion, as well—

03:06.160 --> 03:08.190
Yeah, that's the expected reaction.

03:09.270 --> 03:12.950
You're the party's subleader,
Silk Amberwood, yes?

03:13.400 --> 03:14.310
Silk.

03:15.320 --> 03:17.430
I have an important matter to discuss.

03:17.430 --> 03:19.950
I would like you to be
present here, as well.

03:20.320 --> 03:21.710
Y-Yes, Your Majesty!

03:24.980 --> 03:27.140
Now, Yuke Feldio...

03:27.140 --> 03:29.060
I'll get right to the point.

03:29.630 --> 03:32.360
I discussed the matter

03:32.360 --> 03:36.670
you brought to my attention through
Benwood and Maniella with our parliament.

03:36.670 --> 03:37.470
Right...

03:37.790 --> 03:41.730
The battle for succession in
Salmutaria has intensified.

03:42.190 --> 03:46.730
My plan is to conquer the dungeon and
claim it as a personal achievement.

03:46.730 --> 03:48.930
The dungeon has gone
unsupervised for a long time.

03:48.930 --> 03:50.340
It was simply kept a secret.

03:50.840 --> 03:52.930
I don't know the reason,

03:52.930 --> 03:57.620
but I suspect there's something in it with a
connection to the Salmutarian royal blood.

03:57.620 --> 04:02.870
Such as, perhaps, the
Scepter of True Kingship.

04:03.900 --> 04:09.570
I also received a letter from Prince
Mastoma that backed up what you said.

04:09.570 --> 04:10.760
From the prince?

04:11.060 --> 04:16.760
Long story short, I've decided that our
kingdom will intervene in this matter.

04:17.060 --> 04:18.230
Then...

04:18.230 --> 04:19.510
I see.

04:19.820 --> 04:22.480
Your concerns and judgment were correct.

04:22.480 --> 04:24.520
I appreciate you making that report.

04:25.080 --> 04:26.770
Thank you, Your Majesty.

04:27.890 --> 04:29.120
How very stiff.

04:29.120 --> 04:32.900
Young adventurers like you can
afford to be a bit more crude.

04:33.340 --> 04:37.410
You've already honored us
with a promotion to rank A.

04:43.290 --> 04:47.790
I'm offering you your reward
in advance for my next request.

04:48.110 --> 04:49.380
Open it.

04:52.600 --> 04:53.800
Master?

04:54.110 --> 04:55.300
This is...

04:59.180 --> 05:00.310
Congratulations.

05:00.600 --> 05:03.180
As of today, you're Welmelian nobility.

05:03.520 --> 05:04.840
Good for you.

05:04.840 --> 05:08.810
Now you're a dungeon count, just like me.

05:09.100 --> 05:10.940
A d-dungeon count?

05:11.300 --> 05:15.600
It's a title granted only to those
most accomplished in dungeon conquest

05:15.600 --> 05:17.950
and the greatest honor for an adventurer.

05:17.950 --> 05:20.680
Congratulations, Master!

05:20.680 --> 05:23.880
W-Wait a minute! What does this mean?

05:23.880 --> 05:26.420
I'm not following any of this at all...

05:26.420 --> 05:28.870
But I know I can't accept this!

05:28.870 --> 05:32.890
I'm sorry, but it's already been
approved by the royal parliament.

05:32.890 --> 05:36.470
I apologize for the delay in
delivering it, Hero Yuke Feldio.

05:37.800 --> 05:41.040
Now, per your report and request,

05:41.040 --> 05:44.780
I've discussed the dispatching
of adventurers to Salmutaria.

05:44.780 --> 05:46.350
With the prince? Already?

05:46.740 --> 05:49.850
There was Glad Shi-im and
the culling, as well.

05:49.850 --> 05:52.110
If it's speculated that a
dungeon in another country—

05:52.110 --> 05:58.110
one that was sealed over a century ago, no less—
has become active again because of that,

05:58.110 --> 06:00.780
our kingdom cannot overlook it.

06:04.010 --> 06:07.760
We're viewing this as a trial
of personnel and equipment

06:07.760 --> 06:11.610
with the goal of a technological
alliance between our two nations,

06:11.610 --> 06:14.710
in accordance with
Prince Mastoma's request.

06:15.070 --> 06:16.210
Look at this.

06:16.560 --> 06:20.450
"Setup and trials of artifacts
used for streaming."

06:20.450 --> 06:24.470
"Trials of adventuring
activities in Salmutaria."

06:25.030 --> 06:27.430
"Temporary establishment
of the Adventurer's Guild."

06:27.430 --> 06:29.440
"Strengthening of cooperation
between nations."

06:29.440 --> 06:33.230
So rather than having Clover
accept the prince's quest alone,

06:33.230 --> 06:35.980
it'll be a national undertaking?

06:36.320 --> 06:37.720
That's right.

06:37.720 --> 06:41.100
Yuke may have wanted to answer
his request personally,

06:41.100 --> 06:44.200
but that would become a
problem politically.

06:44.200 --> 06:45.990
The timing worked out, as well.

06:45.990 --> 06:53.780
Salmutaria had recently approached us
about the sharing of streaming technology.

06:53.780 --> 06:55.380
They did?

06:55.670 --> 06:59.630
I've obtained Prince Mastoma's
permission to begin all these trials.

06:59.880 --> 07:05.140
But if the scale of this undertaking
grows too large, it may cause confusion,

07:05.430 --> 07:11.400
so the trials will first commence in a
remote region under his supervision.

07:11.400 --> 07:12.600
Remote region?

07:12.990 --> 07:17.940
An area of northeastern Salmutaria
known as Death Valley.

07:18.440 --> 07:21.200
I had him build a town there.

07:21.500 --> 07:22.120
What?

07:22.120 --> 07:23.490
Build a town?

07:23.800 --> 07:25.620
The prince is building it, yes.

07:25.620 --> 07:29.120
This does mean you will have
to wait about six months.

07:30.940 --> 07:35.000
We've already delivered streaming
equipment there, sent our technicians,

07:35.000 --> 07:39.040
and made preparations to transport
personnel to the Adventurer's Guild.

07:39.040 --> 07:40.760
All that remains is this.

07:44.580 --> 07:45.630
Master?

07:46.570 --> 07:47.760
What is it?

07:48.090 --> 07:49.770
A king's order!

07:51.000 --> 07:52.200
What do you say?

07:52.200 --> 07:56.320
This is the greatest honor
an adventurer could ask for.

07:56.320 --> 08:00.400
It's just waiting for your signature.

08:00.760 --> 08:02.940
So what'll it be?

08:03.550 --> 08:05.410
I have just one request.

08:05.720 --> 08:06.780
What's that?

08:07.120 --> 08:09.040
As advance payment,

08:09.400 --> 08:12.040
could I get six more of these?

08:12.370 --> 08:13.790
A simple matter.

08:14.090 --> 08:15.790
Thank you.

08:35.100 --> 08:40.110
(Magic Airship Forneia)

08:40.440 --> 08:44.450
Yuke, this is amazing!
An actual magic airship!

08:44.450 --> 08:46.110
Calm down, Rain.

08:47.740 --> 08:49.460
It's incredible!

08:49.460 --> 08:50.870
It really is!

08:50.870 --> 08:53.700
It's so big and shiny and cool-looking!

08:53.700 --> 08:55.780
I-I'm getting nervous!

08:55.780 --> 08:58.630
I never thought I'd get to ride
one of these in my lifetime!

08:58.930 --> 09:04.470
It's one of only three airships
in the world that can carry people.

09:04.470 --> 09:07.060
Wow! So this flies through the air?!

09:07.060 --> 09:08.140
No!

09:08.440 --> 09:13.020
Nothing this big can fly!
It can't be true!

09:13.020 --> 09:14.520
It's fine, Silk.

09:14.520 --> 09:15.890
It flies.

09:15.890 --> 09:18.650
I refuse to believe it! There's no way!

09:19.620 --> 09:21.900
Ah, looks like everyone's here.

09:22.200 --> 09:25.150
Are you all ready to take off?

09:25.480 --> 09:28.160
We're more than ready.

09:28.500 --> 09:30.780
I can't believe it! It's impossible!

09:30.780 --> 09:33.460
Well, all but one of us.

09:33.460 --> 09:37.420
Is it okay for a guild master
to be away from his guild?

09:37.770 --> 09:41.330
No need to worry about
us when we've got Mamar.

09:41.330 --> 09:46.270
A dungeon that was sealed ages ago coming
back to life is a much bigger concern.

09:46.270 --> 09:49.930
Wouldn't Mamar actually
be more suited for this?

09:50.280 --> 09:55.140
I'd last longer if a
Stampede were to break out.

09:55.140 --> 09:58.310
Gotta buy time for you guys
to get away, after all.

09:59.310 --> 10:04.360
If this thing was sealed,
it was sealed for a reason.

10:04.360 --> 10:06.820
Something like a culling, huh?

10:07.130 --> 10:08.820
Yuke, take this.

10:09.160 --> 10:11.220
It's the advance payment
you were promised.

10:11.220 --> 10:13.200
Beecha sent it along with me.

10:13.200 --> 10:14.580
You really call him "Beecha"?

10:16.430 --> 10:17.560
What is it?

10:17.560 --> 10:19.400
Marina, hold out your hand.

10:22.340 --> 10:23.830
What is...

10:24.660 --> 10:30.490
We promised in Duna that we'd make
something matching for all of us, right?

10:30.490 --> 10:34.220
It just so happens King Vincent
arranged something for us.

10:34.220 --> 10:36.720
We'll all match! I love it!

10:36.720 --> 10:37.670
Rain.

10:39.690 --> 10:41.480
It's so pretty!

10:41.860 --> 10:42.580
Nene.

10:42.580 --> 10:43.480
Right!

10:43.780 --> 10:46.610
Thank you! It'll be my treasure!

10:46.940 --> 10:47.670
Rune.

10:47.670 --> 10:48.990
There's one for me, too?

10:49.360 --> 10:50.430
Of course.

10:50.430 --> 10:53.640
Yay! Now I'm really part of Clover!

10:53.640 --> 10:55.740
You would be even without it, you know.

10:57.650 --> 10:58.500
Silk.

10:58.500 --> 11:00.920
- There's no way this thing
can fly! Not a chance!

11:00.920 --> 11:01.940
- Silk.
- There's no way this thing
can fly! Not a chance!

11:01.940 --> 11:03.250
Oh... I'm sorry.

11:03.250 --> 11:05.480
I'll get over this soon.

11:05.480 --> 11:07.090
You don't have to force anything.

11:07.090 --> 11:10.020
Okay, um... Let's do this, then.

11:10.020 --> 11:13.010
If it does end up crashing,
I'll save us with my magic.

11:13.550 --> 11:15.100
Can you put your trust in me?

11:15.770 --> 11:17.890
Yes! Thank you!

11:18.250 --> 11:20.180
Good. And you, Jamie.

11:21.360 --> 11:22.440
What's wrong?

11:22.990 --> 11:24.840
Can I really accept this?

11:24.840 --> 11:28.070
Of course. You're a member of Clover.

11:28.360 --> 11:33.070
But I'm still suspended from adventuring.

11:33.370 --> 11:35.940
Oh, I almost forgot.

11:35.940 --> 11:38.330
I have this from Beecha.

11:38.640 --> 11:39.420
Here.

11:42.710 --> 11:45.080
A pardon? Is this...

11:45.400 --> 11:46.400
What is it?

11:46.400 --> 11:48.550
The king has granted her a pardon.

11:49.040 --> 11:53.300
As of today, Jamie Osen
may return to adventuring.

11:53.610 --> 11:55.300
Good for you, Jamie.

11:56.310 --> 11:59.470
It'll be our first time
adventuring with you!

11:59.470 --> 12:01.780
I'm so excited!

12:03.100 --> 12:05.420
Me, too! I'm glad you're here!

12:05.420 --> 12:06.310
Same here.

12:08.130 --> 12:09.330
Thanks.

12:10.820 --> 12:13.830
I'm looking forward to it, too, of course.

12:13.830 --> 12:16.010
I'll really give it my all this time

12:16.010 --> 12:18.170
so I don't cause trouble for you.

12:18.170 --> 12:20.830
Yeah. Welcome back, Jamie.

12:20.830 --> 12:24.160
You don't need to worry
about your brother.

12:24.160 --> 12:25.580
Just leave him to me.

12:25.880 --> 12:28.630
Please take care of him, Mamar.

12:34.080 --> 12:36.840
Okay, Mamar, it's in your hands now.

12:36.840 --> 12:38.350
You can count on me.

12:41.720 --> 12:44.410
See you later, Mamar!

12:44.410 --> 12:45.600
See you soon!

12:45.920 --> 12:47.050
We'll be back!

12:47.050 --> 12:49.320
Look forward to souvenirs!

12:49.320 --> 12:50.360
See you soon!

12:57.360 --> 12:59.620
All hands, prepare to sail!

12:59.620 --> 13:01.740
Raise anchor!

13:01.740 --> 13:04.100
Raise the mana sail!

13:05.800 --> 13:07.500
Ley lines optimal!

13:07.500 --> 13:09.380
Ready to sail!

13:10.560 --> 13:12.550
Take us out!

13:13.760 --> 13:14.790
Cam!

13:14.790 --> 13:15.510
Sel!

13:15.800 --> 13:17.000
It's moving!

13:17.000 --> 13:18.260
Is it gonna fly?!

13:18.600 --> 13:20.490
Look, we're setting sail.

13:20.490 --> 13:22.770
This isn't an opportunity
you'll get every day.

13:22.770 --> 13:26.080
I-I-I-Is it going to fly? R-Really?

13:26.080 --> 13:26.810
Yeah.

13:29.690 --> 13:33.570
Magic airship Forneia, take flight!

14:00.400 --> 14:02.600
Isn't the view amazing, Yuke?

14:03.010 --> 14:04.720
Be careful not to fall over the edge.

14:05.030 --> 14:07.600
I'm not a little kid, you know!

14:10.650 --> 14:15.690
Gotta be grateful to King Vincent for
giving us the chance to see this view.

14:16.710 --> 14:19.110
You look like you've gotten
used to this, Silk.

14:19.110 --> 14:19.800
Yes!

14:19.800 --> 14:20.950
Lord Feldio.

14:21.760 --> 14:23.570
Are you well?

14:23.570 --> 14:25.060
Viscount Bodeman!

14:25.060 --> 14:27.040
Now, no need for formalities.

14:27.480 --> 14:30.170
Remember, you're a dungeon count now.

14:30.460 --> 14:32.960
N-No, no! You're asking the impossible!

14:32.960 --> 14:35.540
This just kind of happened
out of the blue...

14:35.540 --> 14:39.270
Oh, please. Just consider me
someone you can be friendly with.

14:39.270 --> 14:41.510
No, really, I couldn't...

14:46.000 --> 14:48.060
I didn't know you'd be with us.

14:48.380 --> 14:51.810
I'm supervising the streaming
equipment being set up there.

14:52.130 --> 14:54.250
I'd be glad to help, if you'd like.

14:54.250 --> 14:57.190
I'm an Alchemist, after all.

14:57.480 --> 14:58.920
That'd be great.

14:58.920 --> 15:02.170
Anyway, King Vincent sure is
taking a big risk here, isn't he?

15:02.170 --> 15:03.070
I agree.

15:03.320 --> 15:04.520
He is?

15:04.520 --> 15:08.110
Throwing his support behind
Prince Mastoma's proposal.

15:08.110 --> 15:10.460
It's quite a wager for a king to make.

15:11.620 --> 15:15.090
It means he'll have a hand
in their royal succession.

15:15.420 --> 15:21.250
If someone other than Prince Mastoma
becomes Salmutaria's next king,

15:21.250 --> 15:24.110
it'll make Welmelia look bad, too.

15:24.110 --> 15:26.220
I get it. That makes sense.

15:26.600 --> 15:33.290
Of course, whether he wins that wager will
depend on how Lord Feldio does on this job.

15:33.290 --> 15:34.390
I expect the best.

15:34.390 --> 15:37.620
I can't carry a heavy burden like that.

15:37.620 --> 15:40.740
Niberune, are you looking
forward to Salmutaria?

15:41.020 --> 15:41.740
Yeah!

15:42.090 --> 15:46.120
So am I.
I haven't been there in a long time.

15:46.430 --> 15:50.620
Journeys are the sustenance of life.
Enjoy this one to the fullest.

15:51.000 --> 15:51.820
See you soon.

15:53.620 --> 15:54.520
Yes.

16:00.820 --> 16:01.880
Come in!

16:02.450 --> 16:05.390
Sorry to bother you just before bedtime.
Got a minute?

16:05.660 --> 16:07.080
Sure, come on in.

16:07.080 --> 16:09.260
Is something wrong, Master?

16:09.570 --> 16:13.590
Well... there's just one
thing I didn't tell you.

16:13.590 --> 16:18.660
The insignias I gave you before we set
sail do prove that you're part of Clover,

16:18.660 --> 16:20.720
but they have another meaning.

16:20.720 --> 16:21.780
What meaning?

16:21.780 --> 16:24.650
Well...
it's in name only, of course, but...

16:24.650 --> 16:28.780
they mark you as property of
Dungeon Count Yuke Feldio.

16:28.780 --> 16:30.410
Property?

16:30.750 --> 16:33.290
Again, in name only, of course!

16:34.710 --> 16:39.010
As you all know, Salmutaria
is a male-dominated society.

16:39.010 --> 16:41.420
It has a very clear feudal system.

16:41.420 --> 16:44.430
Oh, yeah,
we ran into trouble in Duna, too.

16:44.430 --> 16:48.760
Right. I gave you those to protect
you from that kind of trouble.

16:48.760 --> 16:51.320
If it's accepted that
you're all my property,

16:51.320 --> 16:54.180
the men of Salmutaria can't mess with you.

16:54.510 --> 16:59.060
I know you guys might not like it,
but please understand.

16:59.060 --> 16:59.920
Sure!

16:59.920 --> 17:00.820
It's all good!

17:02.480 --> 17:03.820
R-Really?

17:04.130 --> 17:08.190
It basically means we're
all your wives, right?

17:08.190 --> 17:11.330
So are we all gonna marry Yuke?!

17:11.620 --> 17:12.290
Marry?!

17:13.040 --> 17:14.200
All of us?!

17:14.910 --> 17:17.380
I-It's in name only, okay?! Nothing more!

17:17.380 --> 17:20.210
If you don't like it, just say so, and...

17:20.210 --> 17:22.430
He's a little too dense, huh?

17:22.430 --> 17:25.670
I suppose that's exactly what
we expect of him, but still...

17:25.670 --> 17:28.350
Yeah.
His insensitivity is just too powerful.

17:28.350 --> 17:30.550
He's hopeless with this kind of thing.

17:30.550 --> 17:32.640
He's always been that way.

17:32.640 --> 17:35.850
That is just what
I'd expect of him, though.

17:36.180 --> 17:36.990
Um...

17:36.990 --> 17:39.100
Nothing, never mind.

17:39.400 --> 17:43.230
Yuke, what should we call you?

17:44.410 --> 17:49.990
As your... w-wives... it might not be
wise to talk to you like we always do.

17:50.320 --> 17:52.490
Oh... Good point.

17:52.790 --> 17:53.990
Dear husband?

17:56.660 --> 17:59.370
Y-You can just call me
what you usually do! Yeah!

17:59.370 --> 18:02.130
Really? Too bad.

18:02.470 --> 18:04.380
Yeah. Too bad.

18:05.040 --> 18:07.260
I have a question, too.

18:07.600 --> 18:12.510
What if the locals ask
us who the head wife is?

18:12.830 --> 18:19.210
In Salmutaria, there's always a head wife who's
in charge of the other wives in a household.

18:19.210 --> 18:20.400
Head wife?

18:20.400 --> 18:22.900
Oh, right, a head wife.

18:23.340 --> 18:24.150
Then...

18:26.400 --> 18:27.880
I'll have Rain do it.

18:27.880 --> 18:28.760
Me?

18:28.760 --> 18:31.030
I think you're the best fit.
You don't want to?

18:31.030 --> 18:33.530
No, it's okay, but why me?

18:33.860 --> 18:37.630
You're acquainted with Prince Mastoma,
and you know the full story.

18:37.630 --> 18:39.410
That's bound to make things easier, right?

18:39.410 --> 18:40.920
I get it!

18:41.210 --> 18:44.480
You're right. Rain might be
the best fit for the position.

18:44.480 --> 18:45.920
I agree!

18:46.280 --> 18:47.920
Then I'll do it.

18:48.240 --> 18:49.890
I appreciate it.

18:49.890 --> 18:51.430
See you tomorrow, then.

18:51.430 --> 18:53.680
Want to sleep here with us, dear husband?

18:53.960 --> 18:57.060
C-Cut that out! Goodnight!

19:01.150 --> 19:02.210
Sheesh...

19:02.210 --> 19:03.130
Yuke.

19:05.320 --> 19:08.390
You were being considerate
of me, weren't you?

19:09.430 --> 19:11.910
That's one of the good
things about you, though.

19:12.250 --> 19:14.170
You wouldn't want me talking about

19:14.170 --> 19:19.540
how you're a noble or how we're legally
married in front of them, would you?

19:19.850 --> 19:21.620
Yeah, but...

19:22.350 --> 19:27.110
That's the bond you and I share, so I don't
want you to feel obligated or anything.

19:27.110 --> 19:29.380
I know, but still...

19:29.380 --> 19:32.050
I don't want to let those
things change how I look at you.

19:32.380 --> 19:34.160
You're too nice for your own good.

19:34.160 --> 19:38.820
You're free to use any added
value I have however you please.

19:38.820 --> 19:40.870
You tiptoe around us too much.

19:40.870 --> 19:42.560
You can depend on us more.

19:44.180 --> 19:46.570
I already depend on you plenty.

19:46.840 --> 19:48.460
I'm depending on you this time, too.

19:48.460 --> 19:50.570
Yeah. You got it.

19:54.820 --> 19:57.080
(A Few Days Later)

19:57.400 --> 19:59.320
We'll be arriving soon.

19:59.320 --> 20:03.960
We'll land on Lake Marsche, and
by the time our bags are unloaded,

20:03.960 --> 20:06.340
the sun will already be setting.

20:06.630 --> 20:08.920
Will we spend the night there?

20:08.920 --> 20:10.290
Probably.

20:10.290 --> 20:13.650
Prince Mastoma's supposed
to send people to meet us,

20:13.650 --> 20:16.220
but I doubt we'll be traveling overnight.

20:16.580 --> 20:21.080
We of the Royal Academy would also
prefer to avoid traveling at night.

20:21.080 --> 20:22.750
We don't know the land very well...

20:23.980 --> 20:26.230
All hands, prepare for water landing!

20:31.310 --> 20:33.840
We're finally arriving in
the Kingdom of Salmutaria.

20:33.840 --> 20:36.740
I wonder what'll be waiting for us here.

20:50.810 --> 20:52.930
What do you make of this situation?

20:52.930 --> 20:56.560
They sure don't look like the guys
Prince Mastoma would've sent for us.

20:56.560 --> 20:58.260
They look like bandits,

20:58.560 --> 21:01.230
but being here the moment
we arrive in Salmutaria?

21:01.230 --> 21:02.640
The timing's too perfect.

21:03.010 --> 21:07.150
I agree. Someone may have set this up.

21:08.720 --> 21:11.650
The ship's far enough
away to be out of danger.

21:12.320 --> 21:13.400
Now...

21:13.810 --> 21:17.360
Shall we catch these guys and
make them cough up who sent them?

21:17.360 --> 21:18.720
I'd say so.

21:19.900 --> 21:22.720
Enough talk. Slaughter them all.

22:56.050 --> 22:56.940
(The Dungeon Count of Welmelia)

22:56.940 --> 22:59.990
Next time,
"The Dungeon Count of Welmelia."

22:59.990 --> 23:01.050
(The Dungeon Count of Welmelia)
